1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:33,508
Shishio Tournament

2
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:04,228
I felt like looking back on how I was defeated last time

3
00:02:05,508 --> 00:02:07,508
Anyway, let's continue

4
00:02:16,868 --> 00:02:21,828
Look man here black moves bishop six one white moves pawn five two

5
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:26,068
Then black can move his pawn here to seven four you're wrong

6
00:02:26,388 --> 00:02:31,268
Why should black needlessly move the bishop when his pawn can just as easily go to seven four

7
00:02:32,468 --> 00:02:36,228
Are you the type that gets yourself killed by moving your pieces around too much?

8
00:02:37,588 --> 00:02:42,388
Huh what could you be talking about you seem like the type of guy that acts like he's brave

9
00:02:42,388 --> 00:02:47,748
But really is constantly checking his surroundings and you still manage to get surrounded without realizing it

10
00:02:47,988 --> 00:02:50,148
Like a bunny about to be eaten by wolves

11
00:02:50,308 --> 00:02:55,108
You don't want my pawn to take your bishop do you but I can take it if I want and there's nothing you can do

12
00:02:55,348 --> 00:02:58,148
Taking the bishop first is such a cheap move

13
00:02:59,108 --> 00:03:02,308
Black moving pawn to seven four is obviously the best move

14
00:03:03,828 --> 00:03:08,948
If black moves gold to six four and pawn to seven four moving bishop to six one won't make sense

15
00:03:09,268 --> 00:03:13,668
It'll be a better route to take my pawn and go to three five and take your bishop at seven one

16
00:03:13,668 --> 00:03:14,628
Meow

17
00:03:14,628 --> 00:03:16,628
Meow

18
00:03:16,628 --> 00:03:21,908
So you'll just leave my pawn five two unattended while your rook five eights wide open that sounds like a great idea

19
00:03:27,588 --> 00:03:31,428
All right, then how about my bishop six one takes your gold six four

20
00:03:32,308 --> 00:03:36,708
How could you even hope to get close to my gold when you can't even take my pawn seven four?

21
00:03:39,268 --> 00:03:41,668
You let me take your pawn five two then I won

22
00:03:41,668 --> 00:03:47,908
But what if bishop four seven takes my pawn seven four then what in that case wouldn't I just go pawn to five six?

23
00:03:47,908 --> 00:03:51,348
What's wrong having a hard time keeping up with my flawless logic?

24
00:03:51,508 --> 00:03:53,108
You need to go back to first then

25
00:03:53,108 --> 00:03:55,108
I

26
00:04:02,068 --> 00:04:04,068
I

27
00:04:04,068 --> 00:04:06,068
Finally quieted down

28
00:04:06,068 --> 00:04:10,388
I can't believe that still works once you've solved it. Please take your seat

29
00:04:13,428 --> 00:04:16,468
So I'd like to know what you think kiriyama

30
00:04:17,188 --> 00:04:23,028
What would you take the bishop at six one or just have the pawn go straight for seven four?

31
00:04:24,148 --> 00:04:24,868
Either way

32
00:04:25,988 --> 00:04:27,188
It's kind of too late

33
00:04:27,828 --> 00:04:31,588
By the time the board had gotten to this position. I think you were already in trouble

34
00:04:33,028 --> 00:04:36,948
Stop undermining what we're doing here that defeats the whole purpose of our workshop

35
00:04:37,188 --> 00:04:41,188
Yeah, but unless we treat it like we would a real game. There's no point in studying it

36
00:04:41,508 --> 00:04:45,908
So in other words, what I mean is something needed to be done before the board got to this point

37
00:04:46,468 --> 00:04:50,468
Then explain exactly how looking at the board as it is provides no help

38
00:04:51,828 --> 00:04:56,628
Isn't it clear to see I mean let me think about it. How can I put this?

39
00:04:57,828 --> 00:05:02,388
It just feels like it's unsettling. Huh? It seems unsettling?

40
00:05:04,548 --> 00:05:08,708
Unsettling huh? What's that supposed to mean? Sounds like you're just making it up

41
00:05:08,708 --> 00:05:12,228
Did you think saying something abstract would make you sound smart? Is that it?

42
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:16,628
Be more specific. What do you mean? Tell us now or do you want me to make you talk?

43
00:05:17,188 --> 00:05:19,988
Hey, what do you think you're doing with my cactus?

44
00:05:23,588 --> 00:05:24,708
Sorry kiriyama

45
00:05:25,508 --> 00:05:28,708
This is a workshop so try to explain yourself

46
00:05:30,068 --> 00:05:34,148
I know you're used to studying alone and don't usually have to voice your opinion

47
00:05:34,148 --> 00:05:38,068
But try your best now go ahead

48
00:05:42,148 --> 00:05:43,028
Well, let's see

49
00:05:44,148 --> 00:05:46,148
First of all

50
00:05:46,708 --> 00:05:48,708
Silver three seven is still on the board

51
00:05:49,748 --> 00:05:52,708
It just really stands out to me and a sort of unsettling

52
00:05:54,708 --> 00:05:56,548
Okay, tell me what else

53
00:05:57,348 --> 00:05:59,428
Well, let me think about it

54
00:06:00,148 --> 00:06:02,628
It seems like pawn to seven four is a bad move

55
00:06:03,108 --> 00:06:05,188
All it does is set you up for more damage

56
00:06:05,188 --> 00:06:07,668
More damage? Come on, it's not that simple

57
00:06:07,668 --> 00:06:11,428
Yeah, I'm surprised to say it but I'm starting to agree with the steamed bun

58
00:06:11,828 --> 00:06:12,788
Steamed bun?

59
00:06:12,788 --> 00:06:13,828
Wanna go outside?

60
00:06:13,828 --> 00:06:14,388
Right now

61
00:06:14,388 --> 00:06:17,348
If you want to step outside that'd make my day

62
00:06:18,148 --> 00:06:18,948
That's too loud

63
00:06:19,508 --> 00:06:20,788
Please try to keep it down

64
00:06:21,428 --> 00:06:22,388
Or I'll have to kill you

65
00:06:22,388 --> 00:06:25,748
I see

66
00:06:26,868 --> 00:06:27,828
Unsettling

67
00:06:28,868 --> 00:06:29,108
Huh

68
00:06:31,348 --> 00:06:32,068
Interesting

69
00:06:34,628 --> 00:06:36,228
Well, see you next time

70
00:06:36,228 --> 00:06:39,748
Yeah, I'll check my schedule and let you know when I'm free again

71
00:06:39,748 --> 00:06:40,708
Okay, great

72
00:06:43,428 --> 00:06:44,548
Uh, kiriyama

73
00:06:45,108 --> 00:06:45,348
Yeah

74
00:06:46,308 --> 00:06:50,228
I was wondering if you might be free tomorrow afternoon

75
00:06:50,788 --> 00:06:51,348
Think so

76
00:06:51,748 --> 00:06:54,228
I shouldn't have anything planned for later in the day tomorrow

77
00:06:55,988 --> 00:06:57,668
Are you free tomorrow afternoon?

78
00:06:58,868 --> 00:07:00,228
It'll just be us this time

79
00:07:01,828 --> 00:07:03,268
That's what Mr. Shimada said

80
00:07:06,708 --> 00:07:07,668
So on the next day

81
00:07:11,428 --> 00:07:12,628
Hey, come on in

82
00:07:13,428 --> 00:07:14,948
Thanks for coming back today

83
00:07:16,948 --> 00:07:18,468
Wow, have you gotten any sleep?

84
00:07:19,188 --> 00:07:20,628
Yeah, I slept

85
00:07:20,628 --> 00:07:21,988
More like I passed out

86
00:07:22,948 --> 00:07:24,068
Sitting at the board

87
00:07:25,268 --> 00:07:26,708
Can I get you something to drink?

88
00:07:27,428 --> 00:07:28,228
That's okay

89
00:07:28,228 --> 00:07:29,028
I'll get it

90
00:07:29,028 --> 00:07:30,228
What would you like?

91
00:07:30,228 --> 00:07:30,468
Oh

92
00:07:31,828 --> 00:07:33,588
I'll have some hot coffee, please

93
00:07:34,388 --> 00:07:35,668
But I only have instant

94
00:07:40,308 --> 00:07:41,348
There, here you go

95
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:43,028
Thanks

96
00:07:43,028 --> 00:07:52,388
One more loss and the next one is do or die

97
00:07:53,028 --> 00:07:54,468
All straight losses

98
00:07:55,348 --> 00:07:56,708
I can't let that happen

99
00:07:58,628 --> 00:08:02,388
Whether I get to play in my hometown or not is the least of my worries

100
00:08:02,388 --> 00:08:09,028
I just need two wins

101
00:08:10,148 --> 00:08:12,788
The sixth match is going to be held in my hometown

102
00:08:12,788 --> 00:08:18,068
Oh yeah, so where is your hometown?

103
00:08:19,908 --> 00:08:22,228
Oh, it's in Yamagata

104
00:08:22,948 --> 00:08:23,748
Yamagata

105
00:08:23,748 --> 00:08:26,708
Uh, so what's it like out there?

106
00:08:29,188 --> 00:08:30,948
Oh, just a whole lot of snow

107
00:08:31,508 --> 00:08:33,188
What about when there isn't any snow?

108
00:08:34,628 --> 00:08:37,348
There are mountains and rivers and some rice paddies

109
00:08:37,348 --> 00:08:38,708
Yeah

110
00:08:38,708 --> 00:08:41,668
And that's about all there is

111
00:08:47,348 --> 00:08:50,068
Well, at least they have some rice paddies

112
00:08:50,068 --> 00:08:51,268
Yeah

113
00:08:52,228 --> 00:08:54,308
But they've been reducing the acreage

114
00:08:54,308 --> 00:08:56,388
There aren't a whole lot of rice paddies left

115
00:08:57,908 --> 00:08:58,788
But listen to me

116
00:08:59,428 --> 00:09:01,748
You're not getting a very good picture of the place, are you?

117
00:09:03,748 --> 00:09:04,548
The truth is

118
00:09:05,188 --> 00:09:07,588
It's a place that would be happiest left alone

119
00:09:08,948 --> 00:09:10,228
And that goes for people

120
00:09:11,348 --> 00:09:12,548
Schools and homes

121
00:09:13,988 --> 00:09:15,828
And even more rice paddies

122
00:09:15,828 --> 00:09:19,588
And that's...

123
00:09:21,028 --> 00:09:21,908
That's the reason

124
00:09:25,428 --> 00:09:26,868
I didn't hear what he said

125
00:09:27,988 --> 00:09:30,708
But I have a feeling

126
00:09:31,748 --> 00:09:33,508
He said exactly why

127
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:38,468
Well, guess we should get started

128
00:09:40,148 --> 00:09:41,908
Can you begin with the castle opening?

129
00:09:42,548 --> 00:09:44,468
You remember the board from yesterday, right?

130
00:09:45,428 --> 00:09:46,228
Just like that

131
00:09:51,428 --> 00:09:52,068
Here I go

132
00:09:53,348 --> 00:09:54,468
King to 8-8

133
00:09:58,308 --> 00:09:59,508
Pawn to 9-5

134
00:10:00,388 --> 00:10:01,588
Rook to 3-8

135
00:10:09,428 --> 00:10:10,068
What is this?

136
00:10:11,028 --> 00:10:12,228
Knight to 7-3

137
00:10:12,948 --> 00:10:14,388
Pawn to 1-6

138
00:10:16,228 --> 00:10:17,588
Bishop to 4-2

139
00:10:19,028 --> 00:10:21,028
Silver to 3-7

140
00:10:22,868 --> 00:10:24,228
Silver to 5-3

141
00:10:27,028 --> 00:10:28,068
They're rushing at me

142
00:10:29,908 --> 00:10:31,988
Shimada's thoughts are like

143
00:10:31,988 --> 00:10:33,908
A raging river pulling me under

144
00:10:34,468 --> 00:10:35,028
Team 2-5

145
00:10:35,268 --> 00:10:35,508
It's a powerful weapon

146
00:10:35,548 --> 00:10:59,748
Five, four

147
00:10:59,748 --> 00:11:06,608
Oh, crap. I was sleeping.

148
00:11:07,608 --> 00:11:10,348
I could have died just now.

149
00:11:12,828 --> 00:11:14,028
I see.

150
00:11:14,948 --> 00:11:16,508
I came home.

151
00:11:18,208 --> 00:11:22,028
Oh, man. My shoulder. My eyes.

152
00:11:23,208 --> 00:11:24,448
What is this?

153
00:11:25,888 --> 00:11:27,648
I feel exhausted.

154
00:11:29,748 --> 00:11:38,228
When I thought about it, that was the first time I can ever remember being subjected to an A-class player's thoughts.

155
00:11:39,428 --> 00:11:42,808
It was like being in a muddy stream.

156
00:11:43,948 --> 00:11:50,768
But I wouldn't retreat or let myself be swept away, so I held on. Desperately.

157
00:11:50,768 --> 00:11:59,248
I'm...

158
00:11:59,248 --> 00:12:03,228
No. Both of us are pros.

159
00:12:03,228 --> 00:12:10,808
It's not a one-sided relationship. It's something that, in the end, we both hope to benefit from.

160
00:12:10,808 --> 00:12:20,148
At the time, Mr. Shimada thought I had something he could steal, which is why he invited me.

161
00:12:21,808 --> 00:12:30,688
As for me, I said I wanted to join because I thought I had something to offer, even if what I had to offer wasn't a lot.

162
00:12:30,688 --> 00:12:37,908
And that's why that day still sticks out in my mind.

163
00:12:40,228 --> 00:12:43,508
There's still something that I want to ask him.

164
00:12:43,508 --> 00:12:55,748
Until I get an answer, all I can do is try to hold on.

165
00:12:58,048 --> 00:12:58,608
Right.

166
00:12:58,608 --> 00:13:05,048
The next day, Mr. Shimada went to Tokushima.

167
00:13:08,248 --> 00:13:13,048
The curtain was about to be lifted on the third match of the Shishio Tournament.

168
00:13:13,048 --> 00:13:35,948
Well, look who it is. You just barely made it, Ray.

169
00:13:37,008 --> 00:13:38,008
Oh, hey.

170
00:13:38,008 --> 00:13:44,808
I hear that everyone's going to Mouse Land the day after tomorrow for the farewell party.

171
00:13:45,228 --> 00:13:48,508
What do you think about that? But, as usual, I wasn't invited.

172
00:13:49,048 --> 00:13:54,548
I don't know why you tell me stuff like that when I've mentioned not to over and over all year long.

173
00:13:55,268 --> 00:13:58,428
I kind of feel like this is getting pretty close to bullying.

174
00:13:58,428 --> 00:14:09,008
Nothing here has changed at all.

175
00:14:10,948 --> 00:14:14,868
I squeaked by with my attendants, and I didn't join a club.

176
00:14:15,828 --> 00:14:17,568
My rank hasn't changed at all either.

177
00:14:18,848 --> 00:14:20,568
I haven't accomplished anything.

178
00:14:20,568 --> 00:14:28,548
You know, the only reason I was able to make it to the next grade was because of you, sir.

179
00:14:30,648 --> 00:14:32,148
Thanks a lot for everything.

180
00:14:36,428 --> 00:14:37,348
Knock it off.

181
00:14:38,108 --> 00:14:39,628
Haven't accomplished anything.

182
00:14:40,848 --> 00:14:41,768
That's nonsense.

183
00:14:41,768 --> 00:14:46,188
You've been coming to school all this time while working.

184
00:14:47,288 --> 00:14:48,828
You make your own meals.

185
00:14:49,808 --> 00:14:52,328
You take out the trash and do your own laundry.

186
00:14:53,128 --> 00:14:54,228
You are a fighter.

187
00:14:54,908 --> 00:14:56,308
You make your own money.

188
00:14:56,988 --> 00:14:58,208
And you pay your own rent.

189
00:14:58,208 --> 00:15:01,048
I remember when I was your age.

190
00:15:01,628 --> 00:15:04,748
I thought, I bet I'm going to be a big shot when I grow up.

191
00:15:06,008 --> 00:15:08,028
I aimlessly held on to that dream.

192
00:15:08,628 --> 00:15:09,788
While playing games.

193
00:15:10,528 --> 00:15:11,248
Reading manga.

194
00:15:12,268 --> 00:15:13,588
Hanging out with friends.

195
00:15:14,228 --> 00:15:14,968
Watching TV.

196
00:15:16,188 --> 00:15:19,068
I never had to worry about paying rent or saving money.

197
00:15:19,968 --> 00:15:23,188
And I certainly never had to clean up or make any of my meals.

198
00:15:25,068 --> 00:15:27,668
So don't tell me you haven't accomplished anything.

199
00:15:28,208 --> 00:15:30,088
You did the best you could.

200
00:15:31,508 --> 00:15:33,288
And I watched you do it.

201
00:15:38,568 --> 00:15:40,248
I wish he would stop.

202
00:15:42,928 --> 00:15:44,628
He's always like this.

203
00:15:46,288 --> 00:15:48,348
Insensitive and outspoken.

204
00:15:50,188 --> 00:15:52,728
I just wish he would stop.

205
00:15:54,008 --> 00:15:56,008
When he starts getting like this.

206
00:15:56,008 --> 00:16:00,808
I really can't handle it.

207
00:16:02,148 --> 00:16:02,708
Hey.

208
00:16:03,468 --> 00:16:04,748
Look, it's cold out.

209
00:16:05,528 --> 00:16:07,028
How about we go grab some food?

210
00:16:07,628 --> 00:16:08,208
My treat.

211
00:16:08,448 --> 00:16:09,468
To celebrate you passing.

212
00:16:10,868 --> 00:16:11,748
It's okay.

213
00:16:12,428 --> 00:16:13,108
Thanks, though.

214
00:16:13,608 --> 00:16:15,728
Then how about going to Mouse Land?

215
00:16:16,088 --> 00:16:17,108
The two of us!

216
00:16:17,628 --> 00:16:18,268
Come on!

217
00:16:18,308 --> 00:16:19,088
What do you say?

218
00:16:19,368 --> 00:16:20,408
Let's go right now!

219
00:16:20,408 --> 00:16:22,048
No, that's okay.

220
00:16:23,048 --> 00:16:24,848
Some food sounds good.

221
00:16:24,848 --> 00:16:35,628
And so, my short spring vacation finally began.

222
00:16:35,628 --> 00:16:41,948
The Shishio Tournament.

223
00:16:42,648 --> 00:16:43,228
Match three.

224
00:16:43,988 --> 00:16:44,648
Day two.

225
00:16:46,248 --> 00:16:48,948
Mr. Shimada is in a tight spot.

226
00:16:50,088 --> 00:16:52,948
The only thing he can do now is hold on.

227
00:16:53,708 --> 00:16:57,368
Plus, he's been spending more time deciding his moves.

228
00:16:57,368 --> 00:17:01,468
One more loss and the next one is do or die.

229
00:17:02,348 --> 00:17:03,648
All straight losses.

230
00:17:04,548 --> 00:17:06,288
I can't let that happen.

231
00:17:06,968 --> 00:17:07,848
Mr. Shimada.

232
00:17:08,648 --> 00:17:09,248
Please.

233
00:17:10,608 --> 00:17:11,248
Please.

234
00:17:17,588 --> 00:17:18,308
Coming!

235
00:17:18,308 --> 00:17:18,568
Coming!

236
00:17:19,108 --> 00:17:20,508
Who could that be?

237
00:17:23,508 --> 00:17:24,348
Hina.

238
00:17:25,148 --> 00:17:26,268
And Momo.

239
00:17:26,268 --> 00:17:29,368
Um, hi.

240
00:17:30,148 --> 00:17:30,548
Ray.

241
00:17:31,028 --> 00:17:33,528
The reason we're here is to get our boxes.

242
00:17:34,068 --> 00:17:34,588
Scratch.

243
00:17:35,348 --> 00:17:36,148
Restless.

244
00:17:37,308 --> 00:17:37,828
Okay.

245
00:17:38,488 --> 00:17:41,488
Just give me a second and I'll get you both something to drink.

246
00:17:42,088 --> 00:17:44,728
What do I have that I can serve them?

247
00:17:45,848 --> 00:17:47,588
Tea is fine for adults.

248
00:17:48,328 --> 00:17:51,848
But what do I give a middle schooler and a kindergartner?

249
00:17:51,848 --> 00:17:56,608
Do you have any tea to go with this Inari Sushi?

250
00:17:56,928 --> 00:17:57,768
Do you have any chocolate?

251
00:17:58,208 --> 00:18:00,308
I feel like munching on something that's sweet.

252
00:18:00,568 --> 00:18:01,848
Why don't you have any soda?

253
00:18:01,848 --> 00:18:08,468
Well, thank you for the sushi.

254
00:18:08,468 --> 00:18:09,968
It was delicious.

255
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:15,208
You finished it?

256
00:18:15,468 --> 00:18:16,688
You really ate all of it?

257
00:18:17,208 --> 00:18:17,528
Yeah.

258
00:18:17,928 --> 00:18:18,748
I ate it all.

259
00:18:20,308 --> 00:18:22,288
Actually, she ate most of it.

260
00:18:22,288 --> 00:18:24,288
I only had two pieces.

261
00:18:25,108 --> 00:18:25,808
So, yeah.

262
00:18:26,248 --> 00:18:28,208
I like the one with wasabi the best.

263
00:18:30,588 --> 00:18:31,688
Well, that's good.

264
00:18:32,308 --> 00:18:33,448
I'm glad to hear it.

265
00:18:34,468 --> 00:18:36,748
Akari and I made the Inari Sushi together.

266
00:18:37,368 --> 00:18:41,008
It turned out really well for girls' festivals, so we made some for you, too.

267
00:18:41,008 --> 00:18:45,408
Well, Grandpa likes the wasabi ones a lot, so we made you some extras.

268
00:18:57,248 --> 00:18:57,848
Now!

269
00:18:59,128 --> 00:19:00,348
Who was that?

270
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:03,208
That woman you were with!

271
00:19:03,208 --> 00:19:03,608
Noah!

272
00:19:07,488 --> 00:19:08,408
What woman?

273
00:19:11,008 --> 00:19:12,568
The woman I saw!

274
00:19:13,288 --> 00:19:14,408
How do I put this?

275
00:19:15,148 --> 00:19:15,928
I, um...

276
00:19:15,928 --> 00:19:20,288
I was wondering if you were okay, because I was worried.

277
00:19:21,008 --> 00:19:22,848
It looked like you were having an argument with her.

278
00:19:23,868 --> 00:19:25,508
It's just that...

279
00:19:25,508 --> 00:19:28,348
It looked to me like you were on the receiving end of it.

280
00:19:29,408 --> 00:19:33,068
And I was wondering if you were okay with it.

281
00:19:33,908 --> 00:19:34,428
Is...

282
00:19:34,428 --> 00:19:35,968
Is she a witch?

283
00:19:35,968 --> 00:19:36,448
Huh.

284
00:19:38,108 --> 00:19:39,968
If I really was a witch...

285
00:19:39,968 --> 00:19:42,968
I wouldn't be in such pathetic shape.

286
00:19:46,248 --> 00:19:47,488
No, she's not.

287
00:19:48,808 --> 00:19:50,068
She's not a witch.

288
00:19:51,948 --> 00:19:53,608
It's not like that at all.

289
00:19:54,788 --> 00:19:55,528
You see...

290
00:19:56,248 --> 00:19:57,748
She's my...

291
00:19:57,748 --> 00:19:58,428
older sister.

292
00:20:00,328 --> 00:20:01,408
Older sister?

293
00:20:01,408 --> 00:20:03,328
Yeah, that's right.

294
00:20:03,808 --> 00:20:04,828
She's my stepsister.

295
00:20:05,268 --> 00:20:06,588
So sometimes we fight.

296
00:20:08,588 --> 00:20:09,608
But it's okay.

297
00:20:10,268 --> 00:20:11,388
We're still family.

298
00:20:12,428 --> 00:20:14,328
It's the same at your house, too, isn't it?

299
00:20:14,708 --> 00:20:15,648
Yeah, it's the same.

300
00:20:15,828 --> 00:20:18,908
My sister, Akari, and Hina get into fights all the time.

301
00:20:19,188 --> 00:20:21,028
And Hina ends up crying a lot, too.

302
00:20:21,028 --> 00:20:21,608
That's it, Mom!

303
00:20:21,688 --> 00:20:22,368
Stop it, Mama!

304
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,688
Mama knows they're still family.

305
00:20:24,688 --> 00:20:28,408
Exactly.

306
00:20:33,808 --> 00:20:34,988
We're home!

307
00:20:35,388 --> 00:20:36,768
The mystery's solved!

308
00:20:37,208 --> 00:20:37,888
Guess what?

309
00:20:38,048 --> 00:20:39,068
You won't believe it!

310
00:20:39,148 --> 00:20:40,748
That woman was raised older sister!

311
00:20:42,008 --> 00:20:44,008
I feel so much better now!

312
00:20:44,268 --> 00:20:45,528
I was worried over nothing!

313
00:20:45,528 --> 00:20:47,988
It was just a brother and sister argument!

314
00:20:48,668 --> 00:20:49,948
Who would have thought?

315
00:20:49,948 --> 00:20:54,548
Very interesting.

316
00:20:58,528 --> 00:21:01,268
But Hina, I think that's probably worse.

317
00:21:02,288 --> 00:21:03,608
I'm so worried.

318
00:21:04,168 --> 00:21:05,808
It's the best of her.

319
00:21:06,488 --> 00:21:07,968
It's Squirrely Sensei time!

320
00:21:08,028 --> 00:21:08,748
Let's watch!

321
00:21:08,928 --> 00:21:09,368
Yeah!

322
00:21:09,808 --> 00:21:11,588
Let's watch Squirrely Sensei!

323
00:21:12,068 --> 00:21:13,428
I'm so hungry!

324
00:21:13,428 --> 00:21:23,608
Forget about that Squirrely and give me some food!

325
00:21:23,768 --> 00:21:24,588
I'm hungry!

326
00:21:25,048 --> 00:21:27,848
In fact, I'm so hungry I could eat that darn Squirrely!

327
00:21:27,848 --> 00:21:47,708
They lived in the same house for nearly ten years.

328
00:21:47,708 --> 00:21:58,288
And yet, when we saw them together, they didn't seem like brother and sister at all.

329
00:22:03,288 --> 00:22:05,828
I see, Rei.

330
00:22:07,788 --> 00:22:14,208
So, that's why you left home, isn't it?

331
00:22:14,208 --> 00:22:23,828
The third match of the Shishio Tournament.

332
00:22:24,828 --> 00:22:31,128
After 113 moves, Kai Shimada, eighth dan, conceded.

333
00:22:32,748 --> 00:22:37,488
And at five o'clock, I heard a familiar tune being played throughout town.

334
00:22:37,488 --> 00:22:46,568
I realized, for the very first time, that the song that was playing was called, Hometown.

335
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:37,011
So tell me what Grandmaster Soya's really like in person.

336
00:24:38,011 --> 00:24:40,411
He really does piss me off, though.

337
00:24:40,931 --> 00:24:44,191
Always looking so young and adorable with a full head of hair.

338
00:24:45,391 --> 00:24:48,671
Well then, if you don't mind, I guess I should be heading home now.

339
00:24:51,491 --> 00:24:55,611
One, two, don't miss the next, March Comes In Like A Lion!

340
00:24:55,831 --> 00:24:58,111
I wonder what Squirrely Sensei likes to eat.

341
00:24:58,111 --> 00:24:58,911
GAM!

342
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:05,011
You know what I'm making a sparklingined fundraiser?

343
00:25:06,011 --> 00:25:08,011
What did you do with me?

344
00:25:09,011 --> 00:25:10,291
Going on?

345
00:25:11,011 --> 00:25:12,391
Al prais!

346
00:25:14,651 --> 00:25:16,051
No!

